cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Learn from Lessons: Turning Coding-Agent Corrections into Verified, Evidence-Linked Lessons"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "HumanStudy-Hub contributors"
version: "0.0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/HumanStudy-Hub/learn-from-lessons"
url: "https://github.com/HumanStudy-Hub/learn-from-lessons"
abstract: >-
  Learn from Lessons reads local coding-agent transcripts (Claude Code, Codex, opencode), finds the moments
  where the person corrected, stopped or redirected the agent, and consolidates them into verified,
  evidence-linked, hierarchical lessons that agents load through a skill, an AGENTS.md block or an MCP server.
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - coding agents
  - claude-code
  - codex
  - opencode
  - mcp
  - human feedback
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - name: "Anthropic"
    title: "The Components of Agent Memory"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://www.anthropic.com/research/components-of-agent-memory"
